WEBVTT

00:02.509 --> 00:03.551
KATARA: Water.

00:04.969 --> 00:06.012
Earth.

00:06.846 --> 00:07.889
Fire.

00:08.973 --> 00:10.016
Air.

00:11.184 --> 00:15.146
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

00:15.396 --> 00:18.775
Then, everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

00:19.651 --> 00:22.487
Only the Avatar,
master of all four elements,

00:22.570 --> 00:23.780
could stop them.

00:23.863 --> 00:26.699
But when the world needed him most,
he vanished.

00:27.325 --> 00:29.786
A hundred years passed,
and my brother and I discovered

00:29.869 --> 00:32.872
the new Avatar, an airbender named Aang.

00:32.956 --> 00:35.166
And although
his airbending skills are great,

00:35.250 --> 00:37.502
he has a lot to learn
before he's ready to save anyone.

00:37.627 --> 00:38.836
AANG: Oof!

00:38.920 --> 00:42.090
But I believe Aang can save the world.

00:42.465 --> 00:44.467
♪

00:48.054 --> 00:50.306
( NARRATOR READING )

00:50.515 --> 00:52.183
Sokka's your name, right?

00:52.267 --> 00:55.728
My favorite prisoner used
to mention you all the time.

00:55.812 --> 00:58.606
She was convinced you were
going to come rescue her.

00:58.690 --> 01:01.609
Of course, you never came,
and she gave up on you.

01:02.986 --> 01:05.863
Where is Suki?

01:06.197 --> 01:07.907
How are we all gonna escape?

01:07.991 --> 01:10.410
We're not. You kids have to leave.

01:10.493 --> 01:12.495
You have to escape on Appa together.

01:12.579 --> 01:13.621
Goodbye, Dad.

01:13.705 --> 01:16.958
We won't be apart
for too long this time. I promise.

01:18.167 --> 01:19.711
( CALM MUSIC )

01:23.423 --> 01:24.549
♪

01:26.050 --> 01:27.594
ZUKO: No one can make tea like Uncle.

01:27.677 --> 01:29.762
But, hopefully, I learned a thing or two.

01:29.846 --> 01:32.181
Would you like to hear
Uncle's favorite tea joke?

01:32.265 --> 01:33.433
KATARA: Sure.
AANG: I like jokes.

01:33.516 --> 01:34.642
TOPH: Bring it!

01:35.476 --> 01:37.937
Okay, well, I can't
remember how it starts,

01:38.021 --> 01:41.733
but the punchline is
"Leaf me alone. I'm bushed!"

01:41.858 --> 01:42.984
( CRICKETS CHIRPING )

01:46.654 --> 01:49.115
Well, it's funnier when Uncle tells it.

01:49.198 --> 01:50.241
Right.

01:50.325 --> 01:52.869
Maybe that's because he
remembers the whole thing.

01:52.952 --> 01:55.204
( LAUGHTER )

01:59.208 --> 02:01.502
It's nice to get a
chance to relax a little.

02:01.586 --> 02:03.129
It hardly ever happens.

02:08.801 --> 02:10.845
Hey, can I talk to you for a second?

02:16.517 --> 02:18.019
So what's up?

02:18.102 --> 02:21.105
SOKKA: If someone was
captured by the Fire Nation,

02:21.189 --> 02:22.607
where would they be taken?

02:22.690 --> 02:24.817
ZUKO: What do you mean? Who was captured?

02:24.901 --> 02:28.404
When the invasion plan failed,
some of our troops were taken.

02:28.488 --> 02:30.615
I just want to know where they might be.

02:30.698 --> 02:31.866
I can't tell you.

02:31.949 --> 02:33.117
What? Why not?

02:33.201 --> 02:36.579
Trust me. Knowing will just
make you feel worse.

02:37.580 --> 02:40.708
It's my dad. He was captured, too.

02:40.792 --> 02:42.710
I need to know what I put him through.

02:42.794 --> 02:45.380
- It's not good, Sokka.
- Please.

02:46.047 --> 02:49.550
My guess is they were taken
to the Boiling Rock.

02:49.634 --> 02:50.677
What's that?

02:50.760 --> 02:53.012
ZUKO: The highest-security
prison in the Fire Nation.

02:53.930 --> 02:57.016
It's on an island
in the middle of the boiling lake.

02:57.100 --> 03:00.019
- It's inescapable.
- So where is this place?

03:00.103 --> 03:02.814
Why do you need to know?
What are you planning?

03:02.897 --> 03:03.940
Nothing.

03:04.816 --> 03:06.734
Boy, you're so paranoid.

03:06.818 --> 03:09.153
It's in the middle of a volcano

03:09.237 --> 03:11.489
between here and the Fire Nation.

03:11.572 --> 03:14.450
You guys actually flew right
past it on the way here.

03:14.534 --> 03:16.744
Thanks, Zuko. ( YAWNS )

03:16.828 --> 03:19.288
Just knowing makes me feel better.

03:19.372 --> 03:21.666
Yeah, I'm sure it does.

03:24.293 --> 03:26.421
( SNORES )

03:26.504 --> 03:28.339
♪

03:34.137 --> 03:35.346
( SIGHS )

03:35.430 --> 03:36.848
( GASPS )

03:36.931 --> 03:38.391
( SNORES )

03:38.474 --> 03:40.476
( WATER RUSHING )

03:43.312 --> 03:44.480
Shh!

03:47.775 --> 03:49.402
Not up to anything, huh?

03:49.485 --> 03:50.862
Ahh!

03:50.945 --> 03:52.488
-( THUD )
-( GROANS )

03:52.572 --> 03:54.240
Fine, you caught me.

03:54.323 --> 03:56.701
I'm gonna rescue my dad. You happy now?

03:56.784 --> 03:58.411
I'm never happy.

03:58.494 --> 04:02.415
Look, I have to do this.
The invasion plan was my idea.

04:02.498 --> 04:05.418
It was my decision to stay
when things were going wrong.

04:05.501 --> 04:08.796
It's my mistake,
and it's my job to fix it.

04:08.880 --> 04:12.425
I have to regain my honor.
You can't stop me, Zuko.

04:13.509 --> 04:17.096
You need to regain your honor?
Believe me, I get it.

04:17.180 --> 04:18.514
I'm going with you.

04:18.598 --> 04:21.309
No! I have to do this alone.

04:21.392 --> 04:24.020
How are you going to get there? On Appa?

04:24.103 --> 04:27.440
Last time I checked, prisons
don't have bison daycares.

04:28.024 --> 04:29.484
( SIGHS )

04:30.276 --> 04:31.986
We'll take my war balloon.

04:34.781 --> 04:36.449
( SNORES )

04:39.160 --> 04:40.787
( BIRDS CHIRPING )

04:42.163 --> 04:43.456
( GROWLS )

04:47.502 --> 04:48.669
What does it say?

04:48.795 --> 04:50.713
"Need meat. Gone fishing.

04:50.797 --> 04:52.590
"Back in a few days. Sokka and Zuko."

04:52.673 --> 04:53.716
( YAWNS )

04:53.800 --> 04:55.051
"One more thing.

04:55.134 --> 04:57.428
"Aang, practice your firebending
while I'm gone.

04:57.553 --> 05:00.056
"Do 20 sets of fire fists
and 10 hop squats

05:00.139 --> 05:02.141
"every time you hear a badger frog croak.

05:02.225 --> 05:03.267
"Zuko."

05:03.768 --> 05:05.853
( BADGER FROG CROAKING )

05:05.937 --> 05:08.439
( SIGHS ) Nobody else has homework.

05:11.734 --> 05:15.404
One hop squat, two hop squat,
three hop squat, four hop squat...

05:19.951 --> 05:21.410
( FIRE RUMBLING )

05:21.494 --> 05:23.579
( WHIRRING )

05:29.210 --> 05:30.837
Pretty clouds.

05:30.920 --> 05:32.880
Yeah, fluffy.

05:35.633 --> 05:37.385
( SOKKA WHISTLING )

05:37.468 --> 05:38.511
What?

05:38.594 --> 05:41.013
What? Oh, I didn't say anything.

05:42.390 --> 05:45.393
You know, a friend of mine
actually designed these war balloons.

05:45.476 --> 05:46.602
No kidding.

05:46.686 --> 05:50.147
Yup. A balloon, but for war.

05:50.231 --> 05:53.359
If there's one thing my
dad's good at, it's war.

05:53.442 --> 05:55.653
Yeah, it seems to run in the family.

05:55.736 --> 05:56.779
Hey, hold on.

05:56.863 --> 05:58.698
Not everyone in my family is like that.

05:58.781 --> 06:00.908
I know, I know. You've changed.

06:01.367 --> 06:03.536
I meant my uncle.

06:03.619 --> 06:05.872
He was more of a father to me.

06:05.955 --> 06:07.832
And I really let him down.

06:08.708 --> 06:10.793
I think your uncle would be proud of you.

06:10.877 --> 06:12.628
Leaving your home to come help us?

06:12.712 --> 06:13.796
That's hard.

06:14.881 --> 06:16.424
It wasn't that hard.

06:16.507 --> 06:19.594
Really? You didn't leave behind
anyone you cared about?

06:19.719 --> 06:23.097
Well, I did have a girlfriend, Mai.

06:23.180 --> 06:25.474
That gloomy girl who sighs a lot?

06:25.558 --> 06:26.642
Yeah.

06:28.185 --> 06:30.897
Everyone in the Fire Nation
thinks I'm a traitor.

06:30.980 --> 06:32.648
I couldn't drag her into it.

06:34.275 --> 06:36.360
My first girlfriend turned into the moon.

06:37.778 --> 06:39.030
That's rough, buddy.

06:43.492 --> 06:45.494
( SNORES )

06:47.038 --> 06:49.165
( FIRE RUMBLING )

06:49.248 --> 06:52.376
( WHIRRING )

06:52.460 --> 06:54.211
- There it is.
- Huh? Huh?

06:54.837 --> 06:57.006
There's plenty of
steam to keep us covered.

06:57.089 --> 06:59.216
As long as we're quiet,
we should be able to navigate

06:59.300 --> 07:00.885
through it without being caught.

07:00.968 --> 07:02.970
( ADVENTUROUS MUSIC )

07:03.930 --> 07:05.765
♪

07:20.154 --> 07:21.405
We're going down.

07:21.489 --> 07:22.907
The balloon's not working anymore.

07:24.158 --> 07:26.535
SOKKA: The air outside
is just as hot as the air inside,

07:26.619 --> 07:28.120
so we can't fly.

07:28.663 --> 07:29.705
Whoa!

07:29.789 --> 07:31.499
So what are we supposed to do?

07:31.582 --> 07:33.960
I don't know. Crash landing?

07:36.504 --> 07:37.713
( SPLASHING )

07:38.172 --> 07:39.715
( YELPS )

07:43.469 --> 07:44.637
( GROANING )

07:47.932 --> 07:49.266
( SPUTTERS )

07:50.601 --> 07:52.311
ZUKO: How are we gonna get off the island

07:52.395 --> 07:53.646
if the balloon won't work?

07:53.729 --> 07:55.231
SOKKA: We'll figure something out.

07:55.314 --> 07:57.400
I suspected it might be a one-way ticket.

07:57.483 --> 08:00.361
You knew this would happen
and you wanted to come anyway?

08:00.444 --> 08:03.614
My dad might be here.
I had to come and see.

08:03.698 --> 08:05.992
ZUKO: Uncle always said I never
thought things through.

08:06.075 --> 08:07.827
But this? ( SIGHS )

08:07.910 --> 08:09.620
This is just crazy!

08:09.704 --> 08:12.790
Hey, I never wanted you
to come along in the first place.

08:12.873 --> 08:15.668
And for the record,
I always think things through.

08:15.751 --> 08:17.545
But my plans haven't exactly worked.

08:17.628 --> 08:19.630
So this time, I'm playing it by ear.

08:19.714 --> 08:20.881
So there!

08:20.965 --> 08:22.425
-( SIZZLING )
- Aah!

08:25.094 --> 08:27.013
ZUKO: What are you doing?

08:27.096 --> 08:30.558
It doesn't work anyway, and
we don't want anyone to find it.

08:30.641 --> 08:33.310
I hope you know what you're doing.

08:33.394 --> 08:35.021
There's no turning back now.

08:45.823 --> 08:47.533
( CREAKING )

08:47.742 --> 08:49.618
I hope these disguises work.

08:49.702 --> 08:52.788
We just need to lay low and
find my dad as soon as possible.

08:55.207 --> 08:57.043
Guards! There's a scuffle in the yard.

08:57.126 --> 08:58.377
Come on!

08:59.045 --> 09:01.964
♪

09:06.427 --> 09:09.680
I didn't do anything.
I'm going back to my cell.

09:11.432 --> 09:13.350
Stop right there, Chit Sang!

09:15.686 --> 09:17.396
We can't blow our cover.

09:19.440 --> 09:21.942
I've had it with your unruly behavior.

09:22.026 --> 09:23.527
What did I do?

09:23.611 --> 09:26.864
He wants to know what he did.
Isn't that cute?

09:30.117 --> 09:33.120
- Uh, yeah, very cute, sir.
- Super cute.

09:33.871 --> 09:37.124
You didn't bow down
when I walked by, Chit Sang.

09:37.208 --> 09:39.585
What? That's not a prison rule.

09:39.668 --> 09:40.836
Do it!

09:41.879 --> 09:42.963
Make me.

09:47.426 --> 09:49.386
( INDISTINCT CHATTER )

09:50.971 --> 09:53.140
( FIRE RUMBLING )

09:57.770 --> 09:59.146
( CLUCKS TONGUE )

09:59.230 --> 10:03.275
Firebending is prohibited.
You're goin' in the cooler.

10:04.985 --> 10:07.154
You! Help me take him in.

10:07.780 --> 10:09.448
Meet back here in an hour.

10:09.824 --> 10:13.244
♪

10:20.835 --> 10:22.962
The warden will deal with you soon.

10:23.045 --> 10:24.171
( GROANS )

10:27.633 --> 10:29.593
Can you believe this guy?

10:29.677 --> 10:31.887
Prisoners! Am I right?

10:31.971 --> 10:33.889
( GROWLS ) Tell me about it.

10:33.973 --> 10:36.142
( INDISTINCT CHATTER )

10:37.017 --> 10:39.145
Ha-ha! Hey, new guy!

10:39.228 --> 10:41.564
I know it's the rule to have
your helmet on at all times,

10:41.647 --> 10:43.149
but this is the lounge.

10:43.232 --> 10:44.483
Relax!

10:44.567 --> 10:46.485
But what if there's an incident?

10:46.569 --> 10:48.988
If I'm not prepared, someone
could strike me on the head.

10:49.071 --> 10:54.076
( LAUGHTER )

10:54.160 --> 10:56.495
Give it a week. He'll loosen up.

10:57.163 --> 10:58.789
Can the new guy ask you veterans

10:58.873 --> 11:00.457
a few questions about the prison?

11:00.541 --> 11:03.669
No, you can't date the female guards.

11:03.794 --> 11:06.297
Trust me, you don't want to.

11:06.380 --> 11:07.756
-( SMACK )
-( LAUGHS )

11:07.840 --> 11:09.633
No, that's not it.

11:09.717 --> 11:11.427
The Boiling Rock.

11:11.510 --> 11:14.263
It holds the Fire Nation's
most dangerous criminals, right?

11:15.389 --> 11:17.266
So what about war prisoners?

11:19.935 --> 11:21.437
( OMINOUS MUSIC )

11:21.520 --> 11:24.565
♪

11:27.568 --> 11:29.570
( WHOOSH )

11:33.532 --> 11:35.201
( PANTS )

11:38.412 --> 11:40.372
It sure looks cold in there.

11:40.456 --> 11:42.708
That's why we call it the cooler.

11:42.791 --> 11:44.668
He won't be firebending in there.

11:44.752 --> 11:45.794
( FOOTSTEPS )

11:45.878 --> 11:47.713
It's the warden! Look alive!

11:47.796 --> 11:49.798
♪

11:52.593 --> 11:57.097
So, Chit Sang, I hear you used
firebending to try to escape.

11:57.181 --> 11:58.557
You should know better.

11:58.641 --> 12:00.976
I wasn't trying to escape.

12:01.060 --> 12:03.812
MALE GUARD: He's lying!
I saw him with my own eyes.

12:04.688 --> 12:07.691
No one has ever, ever escaped from here.

12:07.775 --> 12:10.027
I'd sooner jump in the boiling lake myself

12:10.110 --> 12:12.029
than let that record fall.

12:12.112 --> 12:13.989
Don't forget it.

12:14.073 --> 12:15.991
Now go back to your shivering.

12:16.617 --> 12:18.744
-( DOOR SHUTS )
-( SHIVERING )

12:20.746 --> 12:22.748
( INDISTINCT CHATTER )

12:24.625 --> 12:28.545
Hey, there, fellow guard. How goes it?

12:28.629 --> 12:29.672
Zuko?

12:29.755 --> 12:30.798
Shh!

12:30.923 --> 12:33.092
Listen, I asked around the lounge.

12:33.175 --> 12:35.469
There are no Water Tribe prisoners.

12:35.552 --> 12:37.304
I'm afraid your father's not here.

12:37.388 --> 12:38.847
What? Are you sure?

12:38.931 --> 12:40.266
Did you double check?

12:40.349 --> 12:42.226
Yeah, I'm sure.

12:42.309 --> 12:44.937
No. No!

12:45.312 --> 12:46.897
I'm really sorry, Sokka.

12:47.022 --> 12:49.566
So we came all this way for nothing?

12:49.650 --> 12:51.735
I failed... again.

12:52.444 --> 12:54.238
Ah, what would Uncle say?

12:56.448 --> 12:59.952
Sometimes clouds have two sides,
a dark and light,

13:00.035 --> 13:02.162
and a silver lining in between.

13:02.246 --> 13:03.998
It's like a silver sandwich.

13:04.081 --> 13:09.461
So when life seems hard,
take a bite out of the silver sandwich.

13:11.839 --> 13:13.799
Maybe we haven't failed after all!

13:13.882 --> 13:16.635
That's the spirit!
I can't believe that worked.

13:16.719 --> 13:18.554
I didn't even know what I was saying.

13:18.637 --> 13:20.264
No, what you said made no sense at all.

13:20.347 --> 13:21.390
But look!

13:22.057 --> 13:23.434
It's Suki!

13:23.517 --> 13:25.185
MALE GUARD: Prisoners! Back in your cells!

13:25.269 --> 13:27.313
( BELL RINGING )

13:29.106 --> 13:30.357
( WHIRRING )

13:32.318 --> 13:34.320
( MOPPING SOUNDS )

13:39.867 --> 13:42.578
( DOOR OPENS AND SHUTS )

13:42.661 --> 13:45.289
What is it? Did I do something wrong?

13:45.372 --> 13:46.957
You mean you don't recognize me?

13:47.041 --> 13:49.168
You people all look the same to me.

13:49.251 --> 13:51.545
Oh? Then maybe you'll recognize this.

13:51.628 --> 13:53.797
-( HARPS )
-( SMOOCHING SOUNDS )

13:54.882 --> 13:56.550
( GROANS )

13:56.925 --> 13:59.428
Sokka! It's you!

14:03.515 --> 14:05.934
The other Kyoshi Warriors, are they here?

14:06.018 --> 14:07.978
No. I don't know where they are.

14:08.062 --> 14:10.064
They locked me in here,
because I'm the leader.

14:10.147 --> 14:13.275
Well, you won't be here for long.
I'm busting you out.

14:13.359 --> 14:17.029
I'm so glad to see you, Sokka.
I knew you'd come.

14:20.324 --> 14:21.533
( FOOTSTEPS )

14:21.617 --> 14:22.910
( CLANGING )

14:26.747 --> 14:29.166
Excuse me. I need to get into that cell.

14:29.249 --> 14:30.626
No, you can't go in there.

14:31.877 --> 14:33.337
The lights are out.

14:33.420 --> 14:34.713
The prisoner could sneak up on you.

14:36.507 --> 14:38.300
Step aside, fool!

14:38.384 --> 14:40.094
Hey, hey, what are you doing?

14:41.261 --> 14:42.471
( ZUKO GROANS )

14:42.554 --> 14:43.931
( CLANGING )

14:44.807 --> 14:48.227
( GROANING )

14:49.728 --> 14:51.897
Guard, help! I think he's an imposter!

14:51.980 --> 14:53.732
Aah! Arrest him!

15:02.908 --> 15:04.910
Get him off me and arrest him!

15:04.993 --> 15:06.995
( GROANING )

15:10.833 --> 15:12.209
You're under arrest!

15:13.627 --> 15:15.462
Don't worry. I'll figure it out.

15:18.924 --> 15:20.926
( BOILING )

15:22.970 --> 15:24.638
( DOOR OPENS )

15:24.721 --> 15:26.849
Well, well, well.

15:27.391 --> 15:31.311
I never thought I'd find you
in here, Prince Zuko.

15:31.979 --> 15:33.605
How did you know who I am?

15:33.689 --> 15:37.985
How could I not?
You broke my niece's heart.

15:38.819 --> 15:40.237
You're Mai's uncle?

15:40.696 --> 15:42.030
I never meant to hurt her.

15:42.114 --> 15:43.490
Quiet!

15:43.574 --> 15:48.579
You're my special prisoner now.
And you best behave.

15:48.662 --> 15:51.498
If these criminals found out who you are,

15:51.582 --> 15:55.294
the traitor prince
who let his nation down,

15:55.377 --> 15:57.754
why, they'd tear you to shreds.

15:57.838 --> 15:59.381
So what's in it for you?

15:59.465 --> 16:02.050
Why don't you just tell my father
and collect a reward?

16:02.134 --> 16:06.346
Oh, in due time, believe me.
I intend to collect.

16:11.977 --> 16:13.896
( FOOTSTEPS )

16:17.691 --> 16:19.526
Oh, good. You guys have met.

16:19.610 --> 16:21.612
Actually, we met a long time ago.

16:21.695 --> 16:23.238
We did?

16:23.322 --> 16:26.533
Yeah, you kinda burned down my village.

16:27.910 --> 16:31.288
Oh, sorry about that.
Nice to see you again.

16:35.501 --> 16:37.878
So listen, I think I have an escape plan.

16:38.670 --> 16:40.339
I checked out the coolers again.

16:40.422 --> 16:43.383
The whole point of them
is to keep firebenders contained, right?

16:43.467 --> 16:44.551
Yeah.

16:44.635 --> 16:47.012
So they're completely insulated and sealed

16:47.095 --> 16:48.597
to keep the cold in.

16:48.680 --> 16:50.224
Well, to keep the cold in,

16:50.307 --> 16:52.684
it also has to keep the heat out, right?

16:52.768 --> 16:54.520
Just get to the point, Sokka.

16:54.603 --> 16:55.938
It's a perfect boat

16:56.021 --> 16:57.689
for getting through the boiling water.

16:59.358 --> 17:01.818
The cooler as a boat? Are you sure?

17:01.902 --> 17:03.737
I'm telling you, it'll work.

17:05.989 --> 17:07.699
I walked around the perimeter.

17:07.783 --> 17:10.577
There's a blind spot
between two guard towers.

17:10.661 --> 17:12.704
It's the perfect launching point.

17:13.747 --> 17:15.666
I already tested it out.

17:15.791 --> 17:17.834
We'll roll the cooler into the water

17:17.960 --> 17:21.255
and just float with the current.
It'll take us straight across.

17:21.380 --> 17:23.840
As long as we don't make a sound,
no one will notice.

17:23.966 --> 17:26.134
And bing, bang, boom, we're home free!

17:26.218 --> 17:28.512
But how are you gonna get the cooler out?

17:28.595 --> 17:31.306
Yeah, how are you
gonna get the cooler out?

17:33.725 --> 17:36.645
What? We didn't... We didn't say that!

17:36.728 --> 17:38.272
Yeah, you heard wrong.

17:38.355 --> 17:41.567
I heard you hatching
an escape plan, and I want in.

17:41.650 --> 17:43.485
There's nothing to get in on.

17:43.569 --> 17:47.531
Yeah, the only thing
we're hatching is... an egg?

17:48.031 --> 17:49.449
( SIGHING )

17:49.533 --> 17:51.410
Okay, well, I come with you,

17:51.535 --> 17:53.787
or the warden hears about this egg, too.

17:53.912 --> 17:55.872
I guess we have no choice.

17:55.956 --> 17:57.541
Okay, you're in.

17:57.624 --> 18:00.627
Now, first we need someone
to unbolt the cooler

18:00.752 --> 18:02.212
from the inside.

18:03.213 --> 18:05.215
Oh, I can get you inside.

18:06.592 --> 18:08.594
( INDISTINCT CHATTER )

18:11.847 --> 18:13.015
( GROANS )

18:13.098 --> 18:14.975
Hey, what are you? Stupid?

18:15.058 --> 18:16.560
Watch where you're going!

18:16.643 --> 18:18.228
( GROANING )

18:18.312 --> 18:20.480
Hey, you watch who you're shoving!

18:23.025 --> 18:25.694
I think you mean whom I'm shoving.

18:25.902 --> 18:29.114
( GRUNTING )

18:29.197 --> 18:31.199
( CHEERING )

18:34.411 --> 18:36.330
( GROANING )

18:36.622 --> 18:38.540
I need backup over here!

18:38.624 --> 18:40.292
( GRUNTS )

18:41.126 --> 18:42.753
( FIRE RUMBLING )

18:43.587 --> 18:46.214
No firebending. Into the cooler!

18:47.215 --> 18:48.508
( GROANS )

18:49.509 --> 18:51.553
( TENSE MUSIC )

18:52.179 --> 18:54.181
♪

19:04.191 --> 19:06.401
( GUSTING )

19:07.235 --> 19:08.779
I can take you back to your cell

19:08.862 --> 19:10.280
if you've learned your lesson.

19:11.365 --> 19:12.991
( FIRE RUMBLING )

19:13.075 --> 19:16.370
Yes, I have. Completely.

19:17.788 --> 19:19.331
I got Suki and Chit Sang

19:19.414 --> 19:21.041
out of their cells a few minutes ago.

19:21.124 --> 19:23.752
They'll be waiting for us at the shore.

19:23.835 --> 19:25.712
-( FOOTSTEPS )
- Someone's coming!

19:25.796 --> 19:28.590
Yeah, new arrivals coming in at dawn.

19:28.674 --> 19:32.219
- Anybody interesting?
- Nah, just the usual.

19:32.302 --> 19:35.180
Some robbers, couple of traitors,
some war prisoners.

19:35.263 --> 19:37.474
Though I did hear there might be a pirate.

19:37.557 --> 19:38.642
FEMALE GUARD: No foolin'!

19:38.725 --> 19:41.978
War prisoners. It could be your father.

19:42.646 --> 19:43.855
I know.

19:43.939 --> 19:46.149
Well, what should we do?

19:46.233 --> 19:48.819
Are we going ahead with the plan
or are we waiting another night?

19:48.902 --> 19:50.237
I don't know.

19:50.320 --> 19:52.739
Is it right for me to risk Suki's freedom,

19:52.823 --> 19:54.116
all of our freedom,

19:54.199 --> 19:56.451
on the slim chance
that my dad is gonna show up?

19:56.535 --> 19:57.828
It's your call, Sokka.

19:59.788 --> 20:01.081
( BOILING )

20:01.164 --> 20:03.500
♪

20:08.422 --> 20:10.424
Took you guys long enough.

20:10.507 --> 20:12.175
This here's my girl and my best buddy.

20:12.259 --> 20:13.385
They're coming, too.

20:13.468 --> 20:15.762
Fine. Everybody in the cooler.

20:15.846 --> 20:16.888
Let's go.

20:17.013 --> 20:19.015
♪

20:25.439 --> 20:26.773
Are you sure you wanna go?

20:26.898 --> 20:29.151
You're the one who said
you wanted to redeem yourself,

20:29.234 --> 20:30.861
redeem your honor.

20:30.944 --> 20:32.988
Rescuing your dad is your chance.

20:33.071 --> 20:34.364
Your dad?

20:35.323 --> 20:37.993
If I had just cut my losses
at the invasion,

20:38.076 --> 20:40.370
maybe we wouldn't be in this mess.

20:40.454 --> 20:41.913
Maybe sometimes it's just better

20:41.997 --> 20:43.749
to call it quits before you fail.

20:43.832 --> 20:45.041
No, it's not.

20:45.167 --> 20:47.043
Look, Sokka, you're going to fail a lot

20:47.127 --> 20:48.587
before things work out.

20:48.670 --> 20:50.714
That's supposed to make me feel better?

20:50.797 --> 20:52.340
Even though you'll probably fail

20:52.424 --> 20:54.342
over and over and over again...

20:54.426 --> 20:58.138
- Seriously, not helping.
-...you have to try every time.

20:58.221 --> 21:01.183
You can't quit because
you're afraid you might fail.

21:01.266 --> 21:04.644
Hey, if you two are done cuddling,
can we get a move on?

21:05.896 --> 21:07.939
No, I'm staying.

21:08.023 --> 21:12.110
You guys go. You've been here long enough.

21:12.194 --> 21:14.237
I'm not leaving without you, Sokka.

21:14.321 --> 21:15.655
I'm staying, too.

21:15.739 --> 21:17.491
Not me. I'm out.

21:17.574 --> 21:18.825
Let's roll, baby.

21:18.909 --> 21:20.285
( SPLASH )

21:20.869 --> 21:23.121
ZUKO: We gave up
our only chance of escaping.

21:23.997 --> 21:26.750
I hope we haven't
just made a huge mistake.

21:31.379 --> 21:32.798
( BOILING )

21:37.677 --> 21:40.180
Ah, this current is so slow.

21:41.681 --> 21:43.683
I can use this to paddle.

21:43.767 --> 21:44.976
( GRUNTS )

21:46.102 --> 21:48.772
( SIZZLING )

21:49.439 --> 21:51.942
( SCREAMS )

21:53.985 --> 21:55.862
( BELL CLANGING )

21:56.988 --> 22:00.575
Guards, secure the perimeter
and lock down the prisoners!

22:00.659 --> 22:01.743
Now!

22:02.702 --> 22:04.579
( FIRE RUMBLING )

22:07.833 --> 22:10.252
The plan failed! They're caught!

22:11.044 --> 22:13.839
Get the fugitives
and throw them in the cooler!

22:13.922 --> 22:16.299
Uh, they are in a cooler, sir.

22:16.383 --> 22:19.302
One that's bolted down
and not floating in the water!

22:19.386 --> 22:22.681
This is a lockdown!
We have new prisoners arriving.

22:22.764 --> 22:25.433
Everything must be completely secure.

22:25.517 --> 22:26.852
( CLANKING )

22:28.478 --> 22:30.146
( SPLASH )

22:30.230 --> 22:31.439
( TENSE MUSIC )

22:31.523 --> 22:33.233
♪

22:38.446 --> 22:40.031
The gondola's moving.

22:40.115 --> 22:43.660
( WHIRRING )

22:43.743 --> 22:46.121
♪

22:50.584 --> 22:51.835
This is it.

22:55.130 --> 22:56.673
( CLANK )

22:56.756 --> 22:59.593
If my dad's not there,
we risked everything for nothing.

22:59.676 --> 23:01.011
We had to.

23:02.095 --> 23:03.889
Come on, come on!

23:04.431 --> 23:05.765
( CLANK )

23:07.183 --> 23:08.351
ZUKO: Is that him?

23:08.435 --> 23:11.021
My dad doesn't have a nose ring.

23:14.065 --> 23:15.317
Where is he?

23:18.570 --> 23:20.864
That's it? That can't be it.

23:20.947 --> 23:22.449
I'm sorry, Sokka.

23:22.532 --> 23:24.159
Oh, no!

23:24.409 --> 23:27.579
MALE GUARD: Hey, you! Get off the gondola!

23:27.662 --> 23:31.166
♪

23:39.341 --> 23:40.467
Dad.

23:51.199 --> 23:54.202
( MALE VOCALIZING DRUMBEATS )

24:02.836 --> 24:04.838
♪

24:17.600 --> 24:19.602
♪
